            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process in which a relatively unspecialized hemopoietic precursor cell acquires the specialized features of a leukocyte. A leukocyte is an achromatic cell of the myeloid or lymphoid lineages capable of ameboid movement, found in blood or other tissue.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>immune cell differentiation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>leucocyte differentiation</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>leukocyte differentiation</rdfs:label>
