            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any process that stops, prevents, or reduces the frequency, rate or extent of microtubule depolymerization; prevention of depolymerization of a microtubule can result from binding by &apos;capping&apos; at the plus end (e.g. by interaction with another cellular protein of structure) or by exposing microtubules to a stabilizing drug such as taxol.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>down regulation of microtubule depolymerization</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>down-regulation of microtubule depolymerization</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
