            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A form of programmed cell death induced by external or internal signals that trigger the activity of proteolytic caspases, whose actions dismantle a striated muscle cell and result in its death. Striated muscle cells make up striated muscle fibers which are divided by transverse bands into striations.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>striated muscle cell apoptosis</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>striated muscle cell apoptotic process</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
