        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cellular transport process in which transported substances are moved in membrane-bounded vesicles; transported substances are enclosed in the vesicle lumen or located in the vesicle membrane. The process begins with a step that directs a substance to the forming vesicle, and includes vesicle budding and coating. Vesicles are then targeted to, and fuse with, an acceptor membrane.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>vesicle transport</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>vesicular transport</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>nonselective vesicle transport</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>protein sorting along secretory pathway</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>vesicle trafficking</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>vesicle-mediated transport</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
