            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Progression of the exocrine system over time, from its formation to a mature structure. The exocrine system is a system of hormones and glands, where the glands secrete straight to a target site via ducts or tubes. The human exocrine system includes the salivary glands, sweat glands and many glands of the digestive system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:label>exocrine system development</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0035272"/>
